(Previous ascensions: Barbarian, Valkyrie, Rogue, Priest)

This one was pretty straightforward, compared to my others. I found an
altar on DL7 and set up a base there that I'd end up using the whole
game. Did a lot of summoning and saccing, got crowned fairly early but
it ended up working out OK. I went with Battleaxe as my weapon of
choice with this character, since they're the best-damaging weapon they
can reach Skilled proficiency in. An armor shop somewhere in the first
10 levels yielded some Boots of Speed, and I found a Magic Marker in
the Gnome Mines. Found a corpse fairly early that had a whole lot of
arrows on it and a Wand of Wishing with no charges left, so I broke the
wand and got a Blessed Book of Identify, which proved incredibly
helpful. Magic Mapped to find the Vault (you know, Croseus' lair,
whatever that's called), and paid for protection. From there it was
pretty standard gameplay up until Medusa. I still hadn't found a Ring
of Levitation (or any similar boots), so I went back up and did the big
Polypile at my base on 7, still yielding no means of levitation except
for 2 potions. So, I went ahead and just dug under and came up from
below to kill Medusa. Got my Levitation ring at the Castle, but
surprisingly, by the time I got there, I had everything I needed for my
ascension kit except for a Cloak of Magic Resistance, which I wished
up. I found a second Magic Marker in early Gehennom, which I used to
finish up my armor enchanting. I took Divination magic as my sphere of
choice, maxed it, and Magic Mapped the whole Genennom, making it a
snap. How does one tolerate it without it? Vlad was a puss (as usual)
and fell to some +0 Silver Arrows. Got down to the bottom, mapped the
vibrator, went up to the Wizard's Tower. I figured I should probably do
something with this wand of wishing, so I got a Blessed Figurine of an
Archon, a Hawaiian Shirt, a Can of Grease, a Wand of Death. Took out
Rodney, and headed downstairs. Only saw him once on the way down. Got
into the basement, Conflicted my way to the Priest, he almost took me
out but I quaffed a Full Heal Potion and let my Archon beat on him
whilt I peppered him with arrows. Got it, headed back up. The
Mysterious Force was as kind as I've ever seen it, only getting hit 3
times and being taken to the same level all three times (wow!). Only
saw Rodney two more times before I got back up to the top, did some
final gear exchange with my treasure chest on 7, headed up. I had some
forgotten spells and 4 Gold Detects, so I confused myself and did a
Portal Detect on all 4 planes, making 'em all a cinch. Accidentally
left my Archon on Earth though :(. Whoops! Got to the Astral Plane and
Conflicted, had a close call when I got trapped between Pestilence and
an Archon, which was blinding/stunning/confusing me. I had a panicked
horn ramming session for a while before managing to take 'em out via
some cold/lighting/fire wands. Got into the right temple, which was
Neutral. Battled my way back to the left, managed to squeeze a priest
between me and Death so he couldn't get to me, but had a bit of a fight
with Famine. Actually ended up fainting and getting killed at this
point, luckily I had a surplus of Life Saving Amulets. It crumbled, I
took out Famine and hastily re-donned another Amulet. Headed into the
left, it was Chaotic, horns, light, woot.

